From: Arty32 build
Subject: [PATCH] lowrisc-eth: platform_driver.remove returns int on 6.6

The cva6-sdk driver targets a newer kernel where .remove returns void.
This tree is Linux 6.6, where .remove still returns int.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lowrisc/lowrisc_100MHz.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lowrisc/lowrisc_100MHz.c
@@ -882,4 +882,5 @@
-static void lowrisc_100MHz_unregister(struct platform_device *of_dev)
+static int lowrisc_100MHz_unregister(struct platform_device *of_dev)
 {
 	lowrisc_100MHz_free(of_dev);
+	return 0;
 }
